{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30233 - PROTEIN:5811",
  "verbalization": "Angoroside-C is implicated in the biological pathway leading to VMRC-LCP through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Angoroside-C acts as a target for Caspase-5, which in turn is targeted by WS-5995 B or 5-Oxobrucine. These compounds are all linked to VMRC-LCP, indicating a potential cascade of molecular effects. The presence of multiple pathways converging on VMRC-LCP suggests that Angoroside-C may influence the activity of Caspase-5, which could then modulate the function of VMRC-LCP through downstream targets. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism where Angoroside-C exerts its biological effects by targeting Caspase-5, which may serve as a critical mediator in the interaction with VMRC-LCP. The evidence supports a role for Angoroside-C in the regulation of VMRC-LCP through a Caspase-5-dependent mechanism, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
